### Document Updates & Implementation Reports

#### ESP Echo Protocol
- **Presentation**: [ESP Ping](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ipsecme-esp-ping-00)
- **Presenter**: Antony Antony
- **Draft**: `draft-ietf-ipsecme-encrypted-esp-ping` (ESP Echo Protocol)
- **Discussion**:
  - Versions 03 through 05 merged the encrypted and unencrypted variants into a single draft so both use the same wire packet format.
  - The ping packet format is now fixed-size and includes a flag indicating whether a return SPI is present (set to 0 if absent).
  - Antony presented a Linux proof-of-concept implementation using `ipsec-tools` and StrongSwan based on a ping socket model. Interoperability testing is ongoing.

#### Implementation and Interoperability Updates
- **Presentation**: [Update on various drafts implementation / interop](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ipsecme-update-on-various-drafts-implementation-interop-01)
- **Presenter**: Paul Wouters
- **Draft Updates**:
  - `draft-ietf-ipsecme-child-pfs-info` (IKEv2 Support for Child SA PFS Policy Information): Successfully interop-tested between Libreswan and elvis-plus (Valery Smyslov) for both hybrid and pure PFS (as well as addKE). IANA code points are registered. Implementers agreed no extra text is needed regarding handling key exchange changes in Create Child SA exchanges.
  - `draft-ietf-ipsecme-ikev2-sa-ts-payloads-opt` (Optimized Rekeys in the Internet Key Exchange Protocol Version 2 (IKEv2)): Interop verified between Libreswan and elvis-plus. IANA values registered. Regarding misimplementations that send both the optimized rekey notify and the SA payload, consensus favored treating this as an `INVALID_SYNTAX` error per RFC 7296.
  - **Downgrade Prevention**: Interop verified between Libreswan and elvis-plus; currently in the RFC Editor queue.
  - **IPsec Delete Info**: Discussion remains regarding an optional text field without language tags. The chairs agreed to initiate a Working Group adoption call.
  - `draft-ietf-ipsecme-ikev2-mlkem` (ML-KEM in IKEv2): Interop verified across Libreswan, strongSwan, elvis-plus, Apple, and Cloudflare. Currently in the RFC Editor queue.
  - **RFC 9593** (Multiple Support Authentication Methods): Interop verified across implementations with and without `IKE_INTERMEDIATE`.

