### Deprecation & Operational Topics

#### Deprecation of AH and IPCOMP
- **Presentation**: [Deprecation of AH and IPCOMP](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ipsecme-deprecation-of-ah-and-ipcomp-00)
- **Presenter**: Paul Wouters
- **Discussion**:
  - **IPCOMP**: Broad agreement to deprecate IP Payload Compression (RFC 3173) due to lack of deployment, kernel maintenance burden, and compression-side-channel security risks.
  - **AH**: Proposal to deprecate Authentication Header (AH, RFC 4302) due to unmaintained/bit-rotting code in kernel implementations (Linux, BSDs) creating security vulnerabilities.
  - Ran Atkinson strongly objected to deprecating AH, highlighting critical non-VPN use cases where ESP cannot replace AH. Specifically, AH protects outer IPv6 extension headers, hop-by-hop options, and sensitivity security labels (RFC 5570 CALYPSO) used in government, enterprise, and service provider infrastructure protection. Saleem Bhatti added that ILNP (RFC 6741) mandates AH.
  - **Outcome**: The WG agreed not to obsolete AH entirely. Instead, the WG will publish a Best Current Practice (BCP) document outlining the narrow, valid use cases where AH remains necessary (e.g., protecting IPv6 options and sensitivity labels) while discouraging its use in standard VPN deployments. Derrell Piper volunteered to author the BCP document.

#### IPsec Challenges in Non-Terrestrial Networks (NTN)
- **Presentation**: [IPsec Challenges in Non-Terrestrial Networks (NTN)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ipsecme-ipsec-challenges-in-non-terrestrial-networks-ntn-00)
- **Presenter**: Minchen Zhang
- **Discussion**:
  - Highlighted operational challenges stemming from 3GPP Release 19 mandating IPsec on critical satellite interfaces (N2, N3, N4, N9).
  - Identified four primary issues: high dynamic latency triggering premature IKEv2 retransmissions, satellite mobility causing endpoint IP changes (where MOBIKE's single-fixed-endpoint assumption fails), out-of-order packet delivery exceeding standard replay window sizes (16–128), and link outages vs. SA lifetime settings.
  - Paul Wouters suggested disabling replay protection if lower layers ensure delivery order and recommended evaluating BEET mode (`draft-ietf-ipsecme-ikev2-beet-mode`) for endpoint IP mobility.

